===============================================================================
1. SUMMARY OF FIXES
===============================================================================
- Finding N1 (FailedDomain can build a verified card / catch-all `_` arm):
  Updated `VerifiedWitness::from_verdict` in `mathd/src/card_store.rs`:
  - Added an explicit match arm for `Verdict::FailedDomain { counterexample, undefined, defined_value }`.
  - Removed the `#[allow(unreachable_patterns)] _ => ...` catch-all pattern.
  - Rust compiler now enforces exhaustive pattern matching across all 4 `Verdict` variants.
  - Added `Verdict::FailedDomain` negative rejection check in `test_unverified_verdict_cannot_construct_card`.
  - Added `test_all_verdict_variants_exhaustive_rejection` testing that only `Verified` yields Ok witness.

- Finding N2 (CardStore::get last-wins behaviour untested):
  Added `test_card_store_get_returns_most_recent_card_in_bucket` in `mathd/tests/card_store.rs`.
  Verifies that when two cards share the same structural hash, `get(hash)` returns the most
  recently inserted card, while `get_all(hash)` returns both in insertion order.

- Finding N3 (with_promotion_threshold(0) clamping untested and undocumented):
  Documented the clamping behaviour in `with_promotion_threshold` docstring.
  Added `test_card_store_promotion_threshold_zero_clamped_to_one` in `mathd/tests/card_store.rs`.
  Verifies that threshold 0 is clamped to 1, causing immediate method proposal on the first exemplar.

